      "id": "2121766590555554078",
      "lang": "en",
      "note_tweet": {
        "text": "The interesting part is that the permission system is listening to the conversation at all — 'auto mode takes your messages into account' means the safety boundary is partly a negotiation now, not a hard wall. That cuts both ways: it's a genuinely useful escape hatch when the model over-refuses, but it also means a prompt-injected instruction in pasted content could talk its way past the same gate. The honest question is whether the permission model should ever take instructions from the chat transcript itself, or only from an explicit, separate consent surface."
      },
